From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.media.speech: recognizer languages, timeouts, UI options, results, state events, Close; synthesizer options, voice, Close

The remaining FIXME stubs of the DLL, done as Windows behaves where a
speech engine is not needed, and with the state Windows reports when one is
missing where it is:

- SpeechRecognizer: Timeouts (initial silence 5 s, end silence 150 ms,
  babble off; negative values E_INVALIDARG) and UIOptions (example text and
  prompt empty, read-back and confirmation on) are real objects, the same
  one each time. CurrentLanguage is the language the recognizer was made
  for, else the system speech language (the user's locale);
  SystemSpeechLanguage likewise; the supported topic and grammar language
  lists are empty (no engine installs any); TrySetSystemSpeechLanguageAsync
  completes with FALSE (NULL is E_INVALIDARG).
- RecognizeAsync and RecognizeWithUIAsync complete with a
  SpeechRecognitionResult of status TimeoutExceeded, no text, Rejected
  confidence, empty alternates and rule path: nothing was heard.
- StateChanged is raised with the new state when the continuous session
  starts, pauses, resumes or stops (not when nothing changes), sender the
  recognizer. StopRecognitionAsync ends a running session (idle: nothing to
  do). Close ends the session and later StartAsync, CompileConstraintsAsync,
  RecognizeAsync and StopRecognitionAsync are RO_E_CLOSED.
- SpeechSynthesizer: Options is a real SpeechSynthesizerOptions object
  (word and sentence boundary off, volume, rate and pitch 1, appended and
  punctuation silence Default; out-of-range values E_INVALIDARG). Voice
  keeps the voice put (NULL is E_INVALIDARG); with none chosen, and for
  DefaultVoice, there is no installed voice and the error is
  HRESULT_FROM_WIN32(ERROR_NOT_FOUND). Close makes the synthesis calls and
  Options RO_E_CLOSED.
- IAsyncOperation<boolean> as an already completed operation (async.c).
- tests/speech.c: todo_wine removed where it now passes.

---
